# One Last Job's third mode returning Pacifism (CR 303.4f, 303.4i, 702.16c): the creature it enters attached to is chosen as the mode
# resolves, among the creatures Bot1 controls that Pacifism could legally enchant. Bot1 controls Savannah Lions and Black Knight, which has
# protection from white and so can't be enchanted by the white Aura: the Knight is not offered (`! Bot1.Choose`) and the Lions are. A
# creature that could not be targeted by the Aura is not the point (nothing is targeted, only the card); legality of the attachment is.
# Bot1 draws One Last Job on turn 3 (it is the first of the three cards Otherworldly Gaze looks at, and stays on top).

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Pearl
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Mox Jet
Otherworldly Gaze
Black Knight
Savannah Lions
One Last Job
Island
Pacifism
Island x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Black Knight.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet#1.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet#2.Activate
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Savannah Lions.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Otherworldly Gaze.Cast
Bot1.Arrange(One Last Job; Island | Pacifism)
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.One Last Job.Cast
Bot1.Modes(3)
Bot1.Target(Pacifism)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet#1.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet#2.Activate
! Bot1.Choose(Black Knight)
Bot1.Choose(Savannah Lions)
[Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Stack.Count = 0
Bot1.Battlefield.Pacifism.AttachedTo = Savannah Lions
Bot1.Graveyard = One Last Job; Otherworldly Gaze
